# Himalaya environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (in this directory or at the repo root) and
# set values for your deployment. The `bin/himalaya` wrapper auto-loads
# the first match of:
#
#   1. $HIMALAYA_ENV_FILE                   (explicit override)
#   2. <repo>/.env                          (repo root)
#   3. <repo>/packages/HimalayaUI/.env      (this directory)
#   4. /etc/himalaya/.env                   (system-wide fallback)
#
# Calling Julia directly (without `bin/himalaya`) does NOT auto-load —
# use `direnv`, `dotenv`, or `set -a; source .env; set +a` in that case.
#
# `.env` is gitignored. Commit only this `.env.example`.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Storage
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Absolute path to the central SQLite database. All CLI commands and
# the server open this single DB. When unset, defaults to
# `~/.himalaya/himalaya.db` (parent dir auto-created on first use).
#
# For workstation deployments (one daemon, many users via SSH
# port-forward), point this at a writable location managed by your
# service:
#HIMALAYA_DB_PATH=/opt/himalaya/himalaya.db

# Optional override for the built-in config templates directory.
# When unset, Himalaya uses `<package>/configs/` (the templates shipped
# with HimalayaUI). Set this to layer in lab-specific templates without
# patching the package.
#HIMALAYA_CONFIGS_DIR=/opt/himalaya/configs

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HTTP server
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Bind address for `himalaya serve`. Default: 127.0.0.1.
# Use 0.0.0.0 only if Himalaya is behind a reverse proxy that handles
# auth — the API has no built-in authentication beyond an X-Username
# header for action attribution.
#HIMALAYA_HOST=127.0.0.1

# Bind port for `himalaya serve`. Default: 8080.
#HIMALAYA_PORT=8080

# Absolute path to the built frontend assets (the `dist/` directory
# produced by `npm run build`). When unset, Himalaya looks under
# `<package>/frontend/dist/`. Override this for /opt-style deployments
# where the frontend is built once and shipped separately from the
# source tree.
#HIMALAYA_FRONTEND_DIST=/opt/himalaya/frontend/dist

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Julia runtime
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Number of threads Julia uses for analysis-heavy work. The peak-finding
# pipeline benefits from a small thread pool; 4 is a reasonable default
# for a workstation. Set to "auto" to use all available cores.
#JULIA_NUM_THREADS=4

# Pin the active Julia project so callers don't have to pass
# --project=... on the command line. Useful when running Himalaya as a
# systemd service.
#JULIA_PROJECT=/opt/himalaya/packages/HimalayaUI

# Shared Julia depot. Required for multi-user deployments: the sysimage
# embeds absolute paths to JLL artifacts under this depot, so every user
# invoking `himalaya` must resolve the same depot or startup fails with
# `Artifact "X" was not found`. Point at a directory readable by all
# CLI users and writable by whoever runs `make sysimage` (mode 2775,
# group-owned). Bootstrap, all with this env set:
#   1. Pkg.Registry.add(Pkg.RegistrySpec(url="https://github.com/Wong-Lab/Registry.jl"))
#      — Himalaya.jl is registered in the lab's private registry; without
#      this step Pkg.instantiate fails to resolve it.
#   2. Pkg.instantiate() against packages/HimalayaUI
#   3. make sysimage
#
# Step 3 no longer depends on you remembering to export this: `make sysimage`
# reads this file itself (same search order as bin/himalaya) and builds against
# whatever depot it names, so the build and the runtime cannot disagree. It
# prints the depot it used. `make check-sysimage` compares the depot recorded at
# build time against the one in effect and fails on a mismatch, rather than
# leaving it to surface as an unhandled `Artifact "X" was not found` at startup.
# Steps 1 and 2 still need this env set in your shell.
#JULIA_DEPOT_PATH=/opt/himalaya/.julia
